  "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9x-27}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}-1$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+3x+9,$ and\n\n- the remainder $26.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}={x}^{2}+3x+9+\\frac{26}{x-3}.\n$$",
